Job-shop scheduling problem modeled with tasks and resources;
using the default scheduling search (jobshop2.mos)
or a user search strategy for tasks (jobshop2a.mos and jobshop2b.mos).
Model version jobshop2c.mos shows how to change the propagation algorithm for resource constraints. Difficulty rating: 3 (intermediate)
Further explanation of this example: 'Xpress Kalis Mosel User Guide', Section 5.7.2 Task-based enumeration

Project scheduling problem with disjunctive resource constraints and minimum and maximum delays between tasks, formulated
with 'disjunctive' constraints (bridgescheduling.mos), or
using task and resources objects (bridgescheduling_alt.mos) Difficulty rating: 3 (intermediate)

Solving the classical job-shop scheduling problem, formulated
with 'disjunctive' constraints (jobshop.mos), or
using task and resources objects (jobshop_alt.mos) Difficulty rating: 2 (easy-medium)
